# Documentation Rules

## Mermaid Diagrams
- Always use ```mermaid code blocks
- Include participant labels with file locations
- Use colored rectangles to group related flows
- Validate diagrams render correctly

## Writing Style
- Be concise - no filler words
- Use tables for component mappings
- Include Rust code snippets for types
- Link to GitHub source files

## Structure
- Start with overview/summary
- Use hierarchical headings (H2 for sections, H3 for subsections)
- End with file location tables
- Include "Key Insights" section

## LLM Optimization
- Define all acronyms on first use
- State defaults explicitly
- Avoid ambiguous pronouns
- Use complete sentences for context
